From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] avformat/mpegts: do not guess a stream from null packets

Once the demuxer has scanned for services, a packet with the payload unit
start indicator on a PID that no filter knows makes it add a PES stream
for that PID (auto_guess). That includes the null PID, 0x1FFF, whose
packets are stuffing and carry nothing (ISO/IEC 13818-1).

libbluray blanks the transport packets it drops at the start of a play
item (those before its IN time, of the video, audio and graphics PIDs)
by setting their PID to 0x1FFF and leaves the rest of the packet as it
was, the payload unit start indicator and the PES header included. The
first such packet made the demuxer add a stream on PID 0x1FFF, which it
then probed: the packets of every other stream queued behind it until
probesize was reached (5 MB; 9 seconds of an 11 Mbit/s test stream). A
player that resets its demuxer at a play item that is not connected
seamlessly, as Kodi does on libbluray's discontinuity event, dropped all
of them.

Never guess a stream from the null PID. Null packets without the payload
unit start indicator, the stuffing that muxers write, were already left
alone and are not affected.

Signed-off-by: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 libavformat/mpegts.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libavformat/mpegts.c b/libavformat/mpegts.c
--- a/libavformat/mpegts.c
+++ b/libavformat/mpegts.c
@@ -3208,7 +3208,10 @@ static int handle_packet(MpegTSContext *ts, const uint8_t *packet, int64_t pos)
     pid = AV_RB16(packet + 1) & 0x1fff;
     is_start = packet[1] & 0x40;
     tss = ts->pids[pid];
-    if (ts->auto_guess && !tss && is_start) {
+    /* Null packets are stuffing and carry nothing, whatever their header
+     * says: no stream is guessed from them (libbluray blanks the packets
+     * it drops by giving them PID 0x1FFF, and keeps their headers). */
+    if (ts->auto_guess && !tss && is_start && pid != NULL_PID) {
         add_pes_stream(ts, pid, -1);
         tss = ts->pids[pid];
     }
--
2.53.0

